<title>PHILIPPINES: MANILA FIRM REJECTS TENDER FOR 25,000 T U.S. WHEAT.</title>
<headline>MANILA FIRM REJECTS TENDER FOR 25,000 T U.S. WHEAT.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Philippine flour mill rejected on Friday tenders for the supply of 25,000 U.S. wheat for September shipment, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;All bids were rejected due to high prices,&quot; said one trader who joined the bidding.</p>
<p>The firm had asked price quotes for the supply of 11,000 dark northern spring wheat with 14 percent protein content, 7,000 tonnes dark northern spring wheat with 13.5 percent protein content and 7,000 tonnes western white wheat.</p>
